    "title": "Search for $B \\to h^{(*)} \\nu \\bar{\\nu}$ with the Full Belle $\\Upsilon(4S)$ Data Sample",
    "arxiv": "[hep-ex/1303.3719v2](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1303.3719)",
    "time": "2013.03.15",
    "abstract": "We report a search for the rare decays $B \\to h^{(*)} \\nu \\bar{\\nu}$, where $h^{(*)}$ stands for $K^+, K^0_S, K^{*+}, K^{*0}, \\pi^+, \\pi^0, \\rho^+, \\rho^0$ and $\\phi$. The results are obtained from a data sample that contains $772 \\times 10^6$ $B \\bar{B}$ pairs collected at the $\\Upsilon(4S)$ resonance with the Belle detector at the KEKB asymmetric-energy $e^+ e^-$ collider. We find no significant signal and set upper limits on the branching fractions at 90% confidence level.",
